nding  but not to have mentioned in that budget  anything about the nhs  and now we know why and not to tackle  social care  when we know that these these things  have been heightened so much  during the covet crisis i think the  public  will will be genuinely cross and it will  be interesting to see as dan rightly  identifies  how the opinion polls now  wind out as some of this comes home but  i think the people realize  tough things have to be done but not to  the nhs and its magnificent works  okay let's turn our attention to the  daily telegraph dan uh meghan markle or  i should say that the duchess  of sussex featuring on the front there  their take  is that the sussexes haven't been  informed of this unprecedented inquiry  being held  by buckingham palace into those  allegations that she she was a bully  tell us more  well i mean this is all part of the sort  of the much  broader um if you like psycho drama that  is attending  um the sussex is obviously in the lead  up to the great  uh opera winfrey sit down um  that we're all gonna be all well some of  us are waiting with  with baited breath others of us just  can't wait for we've got out of the way  but  let's give give up for a little watch um  but this is if you like one of the more  serious aspects of the psycho drama  which is the allegations  um that she has been involved in in  bullying of her staff  now her and her allies  will say indeed which i think she  explicitly has said  that this is simply just another attempt  by the  the royal family to smear her  others however would say it's it's a  reflection of  the broader issues in relation to her  and  her character i mean i i've got to be  honest i'm saying about this today i  mean i  i really haven't been following the  twists and turns of  of all this but oh dan where have you  been  [Laughter]  it's all anyone's talking about today  but uh but you know look the reality is  they've done this great sit-down  interview  they're inviting us all virtua